    "question": {
      ":question/id": "27aea463-e23a-599e-b3a8-69c9f97d97ba",
      ":question/problem": "Which of the following are vector fields on ${R}^{3}?$\n\nSelect all that apply.\n\n- **I.** $B(x,y)=⟨x{e}^{y},\\sqrt{x+y}⟩$\n- **II.** $M(x,y,z)=⟨-1,2,\\operatorname{ln}⁡(2x-y+z)⟩$\n- **III.** $A(x,y,z)=⟨{e}^{x-2y},\\sqrt{1-x},1{z}^{3}⟩$",
      ":question/difficulty": ":question.difficulty/easy",
      ":question/worked-solution": "Suppose that $S$ is a subset of ${R}^{3}.$ A vector field on ${R}^{3}$ is a function $F$ that maps every point $(x,y,z)\\in S$ to a vector $F(x,y,z)\\in {R}^{3}.$\n\nWith that in mind, let's examine each function.\n\n- The function $B(x,y)$ is *not* a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$ It assigns points in ${R}^{2}$ (not ${R}^{3}$) to vectors in ${R}^{2}$ (not ${R}^{3}$).\n\n- The function $M(x,y,z)$ is a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$ It assigns every point in the set $S,$ given by\n\n$$\nS=\\{(x,y,z)\\in {R}^{3}\\,|\\,2x-y+z>0\\}\n$$\n\nto a vector in ${R}^{3}.$\n\n- The function $A(x,y,z)$ is a vector field on ${R}^{3}.$ It assigns every point in the set $S,$ given by\n\n$$\nS=\\{(x,y,z)\\in {R}^{3}\\,|\\,1-x\\ge 0\\}\n$$\n\nto a vector in ${R}^{3}.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"II and III only.\"",
